--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI ArchivedPage at web parity. The web page is the
notifications inbox scoped to archived items: the `PageContainer` chrome (title +
subtitle + a copy-link affordance + a "Back to inbox" action) hosting the shared
`<InboxBody archived={true} vehicles rules />`. `InboxBody` is NOT a separate
manifest unit, so the archived inbox body is reproduced natively (ADR-011, no
scope narrowing). For the archived scope the web body simplifies to the flat
day-grouped list (web `isGrouped = view==='grouped' && !archived` ⇒ always false),
with the bulk-action set swapped Archive→Restore.

The page binds a pure `@Observable ArchivedPageModel` (ADR-004 — no networking in
the view) over an injectable `ArchivedInboxDataSource` seam whose methods keep the
web hook names at the Swift call sites: `loadVehicles` ← `useVehicles`
(GET /vehicles), `loadAlertRules` ← `useAlertRules` (GET /alerts/rules),
`loadArchived` ← `useNotificationLogs({archived:true})`
(GET /notifications/logs?archived=true), `restore` ← `useUnarchiveNotifications`,
`delete` ← `useDeleteNotifications`, `markRead`/`markUnread` ←
`useMarkNotificationsRead`/`useMarkNotificationsUnread`.

Regions reproduced (every web region, same data + grouping + order):
  • Chrome      — TSPageTitle + subtitle + TSCopyButton(copyLink) + Back-to-inbox
                  (web `<Link to="/notifications/inbox">`, routed to `.notifications`).
  • Filter bar  — severity multi-select chips (Info/Warn/Critical), the "All vehicles"
                  / "All rules" single-selects, and the message search
                  (web `NotificationFilterBar`).
  • Bulk toolbar— selection count + noun + Restore + Delete (confirmation) + Clear
                  (web `BulkActionsToolbar`, archived action set).
  • List header — select-all tri-state checkbox + "{n} notifications"
                  (web `selectAllVisible` + `notifications.inbox.countLabel`).
  • Day list    — "Today" / "Yesterday" / dated buckets of newest-first rows
                  (web `groupByDay`), each `ArchivedNotificationRowView`
                  (selection checkbox, severity badge, time, vehicle + rule context,
                  title bold-when-unread, message, mark-read/unread + restore quick
                  actions, an unread accent bar, and a context menu mirroring the web
                  row menu).
  • Data states — loading skeletons / archived-empty / error+Retry, each inside the
                  GlassPanel; the filter bar + bulk toolbar render above regardless,
                  exactly like the web (no region ever blank, ADR-011).

The web `groupByDay` (Today/Yesterday/local-day buckets), the `ruleMap`/`vehicleMap`
enrichment (`severity = rule?.severity ?? log.severity ?? 'info'`, vehicle via
`rule.vehicle_id`), the filter predicate (severity / read / vehicle / rule / search),
and the `useBulkSelection.masterState` tri-state are ported verbatim into the pure,
harness-verified `NotificationInboxFormat` + `ArchivedPageModel`. No SI units exist
on this surface (timestamps + text only); times format at the render boundary via
`NotificationInboxFormat.rowTime` (locale `DateFormatter`). Adaptive (ADR-002/006):
the chrome actions + the filter controls reflow for macOS / iPad regular width vs.
compact iPhone. All visible copy resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key
names; a11y labels/traits on every control, VoiceOver-combined rows, Dynamic Type,
light/dark via design tokens.

Files (Sources/Features/Notifications/): NotificationInboxModels.swift,
NotificationInboxFormat.swift, ArchivedPageModel.swift, ArchivedPageModel.Sample.swift,
ArchivedPage.swift, ArchivedPage.Sections.swift, ArchivedInboxRows.swift,
ArchivedRouteRegistration.swift. Edits: App/AppRoute.swift (+`.notificationsArchived`),
App/AppRouteParser.swift (alias `/notifications/archived`), TeslaSyncApp.swift
(compose registration, onNavigate → `.notifications`), Localization/Localizable.xcstrings
(+32 keys). Tests: Tests/Unit/Features/Notifications/{ArchivedPageModel,
NotificationInboxFormat}Tests.swift.

NAME-COLLISION FIX: the public value types were first named `NotificationLogItem` /
`NotificationSeverity`, which collide with the pre-existing legacy surfaces
`TeslaSync/feature-views/OperationsSection.Adapter.swift` (`public struct
NotificationLogItem`) and `NotificationFilterBar.Adapter.swift` (`public enum
NotificationSeverity`) — internal/public types are module-visible, so the duplicate
names broke `OperationsSection` ("ambiguous for type lookup"). Renamed mine to
`ArchivedNotificationLog` / `ArchivedNotificationSeverity`; the legacy surfaces
compile again (OperationsSection.o re-emitted, see below).

